@startuml agent-builder-config-classes
' Render (from this folder):
'   java -jar ../../../../plantuml.jar -tpng agent-builder-config-classes.puml
title Per-agent config + "override JARVIS" flag\nGREEN = new | ORANGE = modified | GREY = existing, untouched

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam class {
  BorderColor #444
  ArrowColor #555
}

legend top left
  |<#C8E6C9>       | **NEW** |
  |<#FFE0B2>       | **MODIFIED** (new members marked NEW) |
  |<#E0E0E0>       | **EXISTING** - reused as-is |
  == ONE new config key + ONE merge function. No new file, no store. ==
  == config.get / config.set already read and write every exposed key. ==
  == The only real work: cost_efficiency is captured at BOOT, so a ==
  == per-agent one has to be built per RUN instead. ==
endlegend

' ═══════════════════════ THE CONFIG ITSELF ═══════════════════════
package "agent_runtime  -  the config object" #F5F5F5 {

  class Config #FFE0B2 {
    +model / reasoning_effort / max_turns
    +model_fallbacks / cost_efficiency
    +plugins : dict
    .. {plugin_id: {...}} - the EXISTING ..
    .. nested-by-name key this copies ..
    __ NEW - one field __
    +<b>agents : dict</b>
    .. {agent_id: {override_default, ...}} ..
  }

  class load_config <<module>> #E0E0E0 {
    +load_config(path) : Config
    .. reads the FILE exactly ONCE, ..
    .. at daemon boot ..
  }

  class agentd_config_json <<file>> #FFE0B2 {
    "model": "openai/gpt-5"
    "cost_efficiency": { ... }
    __ NEW __
    "agents": {
    ..  "agent-builder": {
    ..     "override_default": true,
    ..     "model": "openai/gpt-5" } }
  }
}

' ═══════════════════════ THE MERGE ═══════════════════════
package "agent_runtime/domain" #F5F5F5 {

  class agent_config <<module|the ONLY new file>> #C8E6C9 {
    +OVERRIDABLE_KEYS : frozenset
    ..
    model | reasoning_effort | max_turns
    model_fallbacks | cost_efficiency
    verify_tool | memory_enabled
    ..
    <b>API keys are NOT in here</b>
    __ the whole function __
    +resolve(config, agent_id) : (values, sources)
    ..
    own = config.agents.get(agent_id, {})
    if not own.get("override_default", True):
    ..    return daemon values
    return {**daemon, **own-keys-in-set}
    ..
    sources = key -> "agent" | "daemon"
    so a settings row can say which
    __ no file, so nothing to fail __
    .. an agent with no entry gets the ..
    .. daemon's values - which is exactly ..
    .. how it behaves today ..
  }
}

' ═══════════════════════ WHERE IT IS USED ═══════════════════════
package "agent_runtime/application" #F5F5F5 {
  class AgentService #FFE0B2 {
    +run(...)
    __ NEW - about four lines __
    vals, _ = resolve(config, agent.id)
    engine.run(model=vals["model"],
    ..  model_router=router_for(
    ..      vals["cost_efficiency"]))
    .. today it passes model only ..
    ..
    .. reads config AT USE TIME, so a ..
    .. Save takes effect on the next ..
    .. message with no restart ..
  }
}

package "agent_runtime/infrastructure" #F5F5F5 {

  class model_router <<module>> #FFE0B2 {
    +CostEfficiencyRouter
    +build_model_router(config)
    __ NEW __
    +router_for(cost_efficiency : dict)
    .. same body, fed a plain dict ..
    .. instead of the global Config ..
  }

  class NativeEngine #FFE0B2 {
    -_model / -_model_router
    +run(..., model=None)
    __ NEW - the whole structural change __
    +run(..., <b>model_router=None</b>)
    ..
    model_router or self._model_router
    ..
    .. two lines, and exactly the shape ..
    .. `model=None` beside it already has ..
  }

  class run_agent_loop <<module>> #E0E0E0 {
    active_model = model_router(model, msgs)
    .. UNCHANGED. It always took a router. ..
    .. It just never got a per-agent one. ..
  }
}

' ═══════════════════════ PRESENTATION ═══════════════════════
package "agent_runtime/presentation" #F5F5F5 {
  class Gateway #FFE0B2 {
    EXPOSED_CONFIG_KEYS
    -_config_get(scope) / -_config_set(params)
    __ NEW - one entry in a tuple __
    + "agents"
    ..
    .. that is it. _config_get already ..
    .. returns every exposed key and ..
    .. _config_set already merges and ..
    .. hot-applies every writable one ..
  }
}

' ═══════════════════════ THE PAGES - the actual bulk ═══════════════════════
package "the settings pages  <<the actual bulk>>" #F5F5F5 {

  class "clients/ui SettingsView.tsx" as JARVIS #E0E0E0 {
    getPath() / setPath()
    cost-efficiency toggle + both models
    .. ALREADY DONE - nothing to do ..
  }

  class "agent-builder ui/settings.js" as ABUI #FFE0B2 {
    __ NEW __
    + getPath() / setPath()  (dotted keys)
    + Cost efficiency group
    + "Override JARVIS settings" toggle
    + per-row "daemon | this agent" badge
    ..
    writes agents.<my-id>.<key>
  }

  class "templates/chat-app/settings.js" as TPLUI #FFE0B2 {
    __ NEW - the same four __
    .. every agent built from the ..
    .. template inherits them ..
  }
}

' ═══════════════════════ RELATIONS ═══════════════════════
load_config --> agentd_config_json : ONCE, at boot
load_config --> Config : fills

AgentService --> agent_config : resolve(config, agent.id)
AgentService --> model_router : router_for(...)
AgentService --> NativeEngine : run(model=, model_router=)

agent_config ..> Config : reads .agents and the daemon values
NativeEngine --> run_agent_loop : model_router=

Gateway --> Config : setattr() on Save - live, in memory
Gateway --> agentd_config_json : and writes the file

ABUI  ..> Gateway : config.get / config.set
TPLUI ..> Gateway : config.get / config.set
JARVIS ..> Gateway : config.get / config.set

note as N1 #E3F2FD
  **Why "agents" and not a new file.**
  `plugins` is already a nested {name: {...}} key in this
  same config, already exposed, already writable. Adding
  `agents` the same way means config.get can already read
  it and config.set can already write and hot-apply it.
  A separate store would have been a second file, a second
  read path, and a corrupt-file case to get wrong.
end note

note as N2 #E3F2FD
  **The config FILE is read once, at boot.**
  After that the Config OBJECT is what everything reads,
  and Save setattr()s straight onto it. So anything that
  reads config.x WHEN IT NEEDS IT is already live.
  Only two things copied a value out at boot:
    brain_model(config)        -> a model string
    build_model_router(config) -> a router object
  Both live on the shared engine, which is why they are
  frozen until restart - and why cost-efficiency cannot
  currently be per-agent.
end note

note as N3 #FFF3E0
  **API keys stay daemon-wide.**
  Absent from OVERRIDABLE_KEYS on purpose. One shared .env
  - per-agent copies of the same secret would have no sane
  precedence, and the redact-for-installed-agents rule
  already assumes a single source.
end note

N1 .. Config
N2 .. NativeEngine
N3 .. agent_config

@enduml
